<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sökmen ibn Artuq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1104</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sökmen ibn Artuq was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> commander, son of Artuq, who held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilghazi">Ilghazi</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> took it in 1098. In 1102 he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasankeyf">Hisn Kayfa</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a>, founding the Artuqid line there. In 1104 he helped defeat the crusaders at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a>.</p></div>
